usage: yodea init [--dir D] [--force] [--link] [project]

Scaffold a fresh Vite React TS app, or link an existing folder as-is.
Linking writes only yodea.json there; scaffolding never overwrites
existing files. Without a project name the folder base name wins.
Flags must come before the project name.

Options:
  -dir string
    	target folder (default ".")
  -force
    	allow a non-empty dir (existing files are still never overwritten)
  -link
    	link this folder as-is instead of scaffolding
